      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I completely agree with your concern that avoiding all local context can seem perfunctory, but the \"pig in the salt pans\" phrase carries specific historical weight that, even with a positive local context, could backfire with the wrong leadership or media presence. Since you already have a trusted contact in the province, the absolute best strategy is to ask them to verify that the idiom isn't used as a playful label for a specific subgroup in the official records, as diplomatic risks often override informal \"hot tips.\" If they confirm its safety as a harmless cultural marker, you can use it confidently; if even they hesitate, a more evocative alternative like \"the thriving dance of our reeds\" will still feel authentic and safe.",
